    "result_text": "All tests pass. There's only one test class in the project (`AcceptanceTest`), and the full `./mvnw -o test` run reports **BUILD SUCCESS** with 1 test passing.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level rule with a points system.\n\n**Changes (3 files):**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `membershipPoints` field to the owner schema and updated the `membershipLevel` description to reflect the new points-based derivation. (The `OwnerDto` with its `setMembershipPoints`/`setMembershipLevel` setters is generated from this spec.)\n\n2. **`MembershipPoints.java`** (new) \u2014 A small, cohesive helper that scores an owner and sets both fields:\n   - points start at 0; `+2` email, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` for a household of 3+, `+3` for tenure over 365 days\n   - level mapping: `1` (0\u20131), `2` (2\u20133), `3` (4\u20135), `4` (6+)\n   - household size reuses the existing `Household.id(lastName, postcode)` key over all owners.\n\n3. **`OwnerNamesakeCountAdvice.java`** \u2014 Replaced the two inline level-computation lines with a single delegation call (`MembershipPoints.assign(...)`) and removed the now-dead `tenureLevel` method plus its two unused imports.\n\n**On structural impact:** the new behaviour lives in a fresh class with near-zero surrounding complexity (`WMC_other \u2248 0`), and the only edit to the pre-existing large-context method (`addNamesakeCount`) is a net one-line delegation, so the costliest lever (WMC_other \u00d7 CC \u00d7 changed_lines) stays minimal rather than growing an existing method or class.\n\nThe acceptance test's case (email + no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure \u2192 3 points \u2192 level 2) is satisfied.",
