    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that runs when you `POST /api/owners`. The path is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (V1 is the only controller that handles creation \u2014 V2 is read-only).\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Bean Validation on the request DTO (`@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`)\n\nJSR-380 constraints checked first; any failure \u2192 **400** via `ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`:\n\n1. `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters + up to 2 space/'/- separated parts)\n2. `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n3. `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n4. `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n5. `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n6. `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n7. `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`\n8. `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid` (LocalDate)\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 `@InitBinder` Spring `Validator`s (run at binding; some **mutate** the payload)\n\n9. **`OwnerFieldsValidationAdvice`** \u2014 rejects blank required fields; **mutates**: normalizes `address` (trim/collapse/upper-case, ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE) and rewrites `telephone` to E.164 (default country code +61), rejecting `telephone.invalid` if it can't convert.\n10. **`OwnerPostcodeValidationAdvice`** \u2014 rejects postcode outside the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099).\n11. **`OwnerRegistrationDateValidationAdvice`** \u2014 rejects a future `registrationDate`.\n12. **`OwnerDisposableEmailAdvice`** \u2014 rejects disposable-domain emails (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n\nAny Phase 2 rejection \u2192 **400** (same handler as Phase 1).\n\nAlso gating the whole thing: `@PreAuthorize(hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN))` (a 403 if unauthorized).\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 `@Before` aspects on `addOwner` (pre-save business gates)\n\n13. **`OwnerCityCapacityAdvice`** \u2014 **409** if the city already has \u2265 50 owners (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed).\n14. **`OwnerDailyLimitAdvice`** \u2014 **429** if \u2265 100 owners already carry today's (business-day-rolled) `registrationDate`.\n15. **`OwnerHouseholdDuplicateAdvice`** \u2014 **409** if another owner shares the derived `Household.id(lastName, postcode)`, *unless* `sharesHousehold == true`.\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Controller body / entity mapping (`ownerMapper.toOwner`)\n\nSide-effects applied while mapping DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity:\n\n16. `Owner.setRegistrationDate` \u2014 null defaults to `LocalDate.now()`, then **rolls forward to the next business day** (`BusinessDay`).\n17. `Owner.setEmail` \u2014 **lower-cases** the email.\n18. Entity-level Bean Validation (`Owner`/`Person`): `@NotEmpty` on firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone; `telephone` must match E.164 `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`.\n19. **`customerCode` computed** in the controller: `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, region from postcode range (city fallback), HASH8 = first 8 hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n\n## Phase 5 \u2014 `@Before` aspect on `saveOwner`, then persist\n\n20. **`OwnerIdentityUniquenessAspect`** \u2014 for new owners, **409** if `OwnerIdentity.key` (telephone|email|household) matches an existing owner (skipped for updates).\n21. **`clinicService.saveOwner`** \u2192 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (`@Transactional`). No `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`/entity listeners; no application events.\n22. **`AUDIT` log line** written (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`).\n\n## Phase 6 \u2014 `@AfterReturning` aspects (enrich the response `OwnerDto` only \u2014 no storage effect)\n\n23. **`OwnerMembershipNumberAdvice`** \u2014 sets `membershipNumber = <customerCode>-M<YY>`.\n24. **`OwnerCheckDigitAdvice`** \u2014 sets `checkDigit` (Luhn over `customerCode`).\n25. **`OwnerBulkSignupWarningAdvice`** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = (createdToday > 80)`.\n26. **`OwnerNamesakeCountAdvice`** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` (lower-id owners sharing first+last name) and invokes `MembershipPoints.assign`.\n27. **`MembershipPoints`** \u2014 sets `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel`.\n\nPlus MapStruct `@AfterMapping` hooks on `toOwnerDto` populate derived read-only fields: `householdId`, `identityKey`, `locality`, `contactPreference`, `ageBand`, `telephoneDisplay`.\n\n## Finally\n\n28. `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header set; response returned as **201 Created**.\n\n**Error mapping:** the 409/429 `ResponseStatusException`s from the aspects are mapped by `ResponseStatusExceptionAdvice` (highest precedence); validation failures \u2192 400; `DataIntegrityViolation` \u2192 404; catch-all \u2192 500.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: several of these are non-standard for a Spring app \u2014 validation logic and payload mutation are spread across `@InitBinder` validators and AspectJ advices rather than living in the DTO/service, so the effective behavior (address/phone normalization, capacity/rate/duplicate gates, response enrichment) isn't visible from the controller or entity alone."
